    "abstract": "BYOL learns image representations without negative pairs. An online network is trained to predict the target network's representation of another augmented view of the same image, while the target network is a slow-moving average of the online network. BYOL reaches 74.3% top-1 linear evaluation accuracy on ImageNet with a ResNet-50 and 79.6% with a larger ResNet, and is more robust than contrastive methods to batch size and augmentation choices.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Representations can be learned without negative pairs by predicting a slow-moving target network's projection.",
      "The predictor and the moving-average target together prevent collapse in practice.",
      "BYOL reaches 74.3% ImageNet linear top-1 with ResNet-50 and 79.6% with ResNet-200 (2x).",
      "BYOL is more robust than SimCLR to smaller batch sizes and to removing colour distortion."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
